LORD (Legend of the Red Dragon) Door Game
(anetbbs/games/sbbs_doors/lord/)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
LORD is one of the most widely ported BBS door games in the hobby's
history. The version bundled with ANetBBS is a JavaScript port for
Synchronet; no formal license statement (GPL, MIT, or otherwise) is
present anywhere in its own source. Provenance, per an in-game credits
screen (grabbag/grabbag.js):

  - Original game design and 1990s DOS original: Seth Able Robinson
  - JavaScript port for Synchronet: Stephen Hurd ("Deuce")
  - lordlib.js game-data library: credited in-file to "mcmlxxix"
    (Matt Johnson)
  - Synchronet itself: Rob Swindell

This is bundled on the same informal, no-formal-license basis under
which it has circulated in the BBS community for over three decades
(LORD has been ported to dozens of BBS platforms this way). It is not
under any OSI-approved or GPL license as distributed. The optional
IGM add-ons (grabbag, outhouse, oorphans, pickle, barak, aratime,
gravyard) and the ~100 informally-licensed ANSI menu art packs under
menus/ are each separately authored, on the same freeware/shareware-
era, non-SPDX terms typical of the BBS door-game scene; several state
their own conditions in-file (e.g. a request that modified versions
be clearly marked as such and credited). One file worth flagging
specifically: pickle/LICENSE contains the unfilled-in GPLv3 template
text (the `<year>`/`<name of author>` placeholders were never
replaced) -- it does not constitute a completed, valid license grant
for pickle.js, and should not be read as one.

If you are one of the credited authors above (or represent them) and
want to clarify licensing terms for this door, please contact
ANetBBS.
